  "bbc6a560-2035-4c00-aa48-ca013ab791e2": "Unique identification, as assigned by the account owner, to unambiguously identify the account notification.",
  "bbf11029-ae2a-4ae2-b78e-f7db65d860f5": "Specifies the details on how the settlement of the original transaction(s) between the instructing agent and the instructed agent was completed.",
  "bc19ef06-4911-442c-aa69-a7c381c9c37e": "Party that issues the request message.",
  "bc226507-862a-4a14-91e1-6d3f01c04cf9": "Weighted average price of the units in the account before the transfer was executed.",
  "bc3084b0-fe93-4573-b174-013bda0eaaa1": "Financial institution servicing an account for the debtor.",
  "bc38320c-6727-44fa-87c4-a3d8a162d762": "Number of units that have been received (crystallised) or not yet received (uncrystallised) from the fund. This is typically relevant to a pension fund.",
  "bc60b0fd-91b0-48fa-b2da-1c0479a84937": "Further information related to the processing of the payment instruction, provided by the initiating party, and intended for the creditor agent.",
  "bc7d2f26-d16a-4469-aed0-4267d236daba": "Unique identification, as assigned by the initiating party, to unambiguously identify the transaction. This identification is passed on, unchanged, throughout the entire end-to-end chain.||Usage: The end-to-end identification can be used for reconciliation or to link tasks relating to the transaction. It can be included in several messages related to the transaction.||Usage: In case there are technical limitations to pass on multiple references, the end-to-end identification must be passed on throughout the entire end-to-end chain.",
  "bc9ecd45-906c-4a4d-b943-d3ea54c70f59": "Original investigation reason as provided in the investigation request.",
  "bca856fd-f648-4226-b434-720e4690a282": "Provides the identification and the content of the referred document.",
  "bcadcafc-cd22-46e9-a8f0-3cf69e4294d3": "Specifies the means of payment that will be used to move the amount of money.",
  "bce3de89-8fee-4a56-92cb-36a5001e133e": "Instruction has been acknowledged by the account servicer but is in repair.",
  "bcf86d54-9c6f-4d19-937f-e8e2186d0680": "Provides detailed information on the cancellation status reason.",
