  "_Ew-kEWi8EeS87LmvcA55sg": "CMAC (Cipher based Message Authentication Code) defined by the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST 800-38B - May 2005), using the block cipher Advanced Encryption Standard with a 256 bits cryptographic key, approved by the Federal Information Processing Standards (FIPS 197 - November 6, 2001 - Advanced Encryption Standard). The CMAC algorithm is computed on the SHA-512 digest of the message.",
